From: BerryMC <148406068+BerryMC@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 11:33:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Add stack traces and async JSON list saving

- Print the worker thread stack trace when a plugin leaves async
  tasks running during reload, matching the existing shutdown-path
  output (Airplane via Gale/Leaf; shutdown path already existed).

- Save ops/whitelist/ban JSON lists asynchronously: the JSON snapshot
  is built on the calling thread (so the backing map is never read
  concurrently) and only the file write is offloaded to a dedicated
  daemon thread; JsonList.waitForPendingSaves() is called in
  MinecraftServer.stop() to flush pending writes. Based on Akarin as
  ported by Leaf. Behind async-json-list-save (default true).

diff --git a/src/main/java/dev/pomf/dionysus/DionysusConfig.java b/src/main/java/dev/pomf/dionysus/DionysusConfig.java
index f671a7fb5ecc416dafffe462941c6582736d3dcf..63b123dba333fe1786bc1018221d2dc7796f25a9 100644
--- a/src/main/java/dev/pomf/dionysus/DionysusConfig.java
+++ b/src/main/java/dev/pomf/dionysus/DionysusConfig.java
@@ -465,4 +465,12 @@ public class DionysusConfig {
                 unlike an earlier FlamePaper-based attempt removed in v0.1.16, this
                 implementation never skips based on block occlusion.""");
     }
+
+    public static boolean asyncJsonListSave = true;
+    private static void asyncJsonListSave() {
+        asyncJsonListSave = getBoolean("async-json-list-save", asyncJsonListSave, """
+                Save ops/whitelist/ban JSON lists asynchronously. The JSON snapshot is
+                still built on the main thread, only the file write is offloaded, and
+                pending saves are flushed when the server stops.""");
+    }
 }
diff --git a/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/JsonList.java b/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/JsonList.java
index 2a259758b5cf1fd66f5300036d0821c554e457a3..d522546f4588d087f2546a91e5cc734c21d87def 100644
